  "wikitext": "{{PageDisplay}}\n[[File:Chicken.png|200px|left|Chicken]]\n\n{{Infobox\n |title = [[Animals|Animal]]\n |level = 1 • 12 • 23\n |price = 20 • 140 • 270\n |gives = {{Infoicon|egg|big|link=Egg}}\n |time = every 20 min\n}}\n'''Chickens''' are [[farm]] [[animals]] that produce [[egg]]s. They are unlocked at [[experience]] level 1. They are the first type of farm animal unlocked in the game.\n\n{{Clr}}----\n==='''Appearance'''===\n<gallery>\nChicken.png\nChicken Walking.png\nChicken Eating.png\nChicken Looking.png\nChicken Full.png\nChicken Hungry.png\nFile:Chicken Summer.jpg|Chicken Summer\nFile:Chickens Winter.png|Chicken Winter\nFile:Chicken Halloween.png|Chicken Halloween\n</gallery>\n----\n==='''Alternate appearance'''===\n{{Main|Themes}}\nChickens wear themed clothes and accessories during summer, Halloween and winter.\n----\n==='''Buying'''===\n[[File:Chicken Coop.png|150px|left|A chicken coop]]\nChickens must be placed in [[Chicken Coop|chicken coops]] to be purchased. Coops cost 5 {{Infoicon|coin|link=Coin}} each.\n\nThey are unlocked at levels 1, 12 and 23. Each coop can house six chickens.\n\nAt level 1, chickens cost 20 coins each; at level 12, 140 coins; at level 23, 270 coins.\n\nChickens and chicken coops can be bought from the [[shop]].{{Infoicon|shop|bigger|link=Shop}}\n\n{{Clr}}----\n==='''Harvesting'''===\n[[File:Chicken Basket.png|left|150px|Egg basket]]\nEggs can be collected from chickens every 20 minutes. Players can skip the wait by paying 2 [[diamond]]s per chicken. Players must then give chickens [[Chicken Feed|chicken feed]] to get another harvest.\n\nChicken feed is made of:\n{| border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: .5em 0;\"\n|-\n|[[File:Corn.png|75px|Corn|link=Corn]]\n|[[File:Wheat.png|75px|Wheat|link=Wheat]]\n|-\n|'''x1'''\n|'''x2'''\n|}\n[[File:Chicken.gif|center|500px]]\n\n{{Clr}}----\n==='''Strategy tips'''===\n* Making chicken feed only takes 5 minutes for 3 units. If you have two feed mills you can easily collect all your eggs and replenish your feed stock by the time the chickens are full again.\n* Instead of collecting the eggs from the chickens every time they're ready, you may decide to let the chickens sit on the eggs until they're needed. That will keep precious barn storage space free for other items.\n* If you decide to let the chickens sit on the eggs until they're needed, you can sell the excess [[Chicken Feed|chicken feed]] instead. Chicken feed sells very quickly at the maximum price of 72 coins for every 10 feed.\n* Eggs are easily found in the [[Daily Dirt]], so eggs may not sell very well unless they're sold at a lower price.\n* Feeding farm animals and harvesting eggs are common tasks in [[Derby|derbies]].\n----\n==='''Easter egg'''===\n*Tapping the chicken coop scares the chickens and makes them try to fly away from the perceived danger. This mimics their behavior in real life: chickens mostly fly briefly when frightened.\n----\n==='''Did you know?'''===\n*Chickens have a great memory. They can distinguish between over 100 different faces of people or animals.\n*In real life, the Hay Day chicken's breed is the Californian White chicken.\n----\n{{Navigation}}\n{{Languages\n|de = Huhn\n|es = Gallina\n|fr = Poule\n|it = Gallina\n|no = Høne\n|sv = Höna\n|zh = 母鸡\n}}\n[[pt-br:Galinha]]\n[[ru:Курица]]\n\n[[Category:Farm Animals]]",
